# Neo MCP for client site edits

When the user asks to change, inspect, create, or fix anything on a **live client WordPress site** from the Neo Pulse Sites panel, use **Neo MCP for that site**. Do not invent another CMS path (SFTP-first, browser admin-only, or removed stacks) when Neo MCP is available.

## Source of truth for which sites exist

1. Pulse Sites list / seed: [`src/components/integrations/default-properties-seed.json`](src/components/integrations/default-properties-seed.json)
2. Connectivity probe: `node scripts/neo-mcp-site-probe.mjs` (draft → verify → delete on every seed site in parallel)

Auth for probes comes from each seed entry’s `username` + `appPassword`. Cursor MCP servers live in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` as `neo-mcp-<hostname-with-dots-as-hyphens>`.

